# Quote taker
#
# Shows:   the client side answering quotes sent unasked — `on quote`, `requoted`, `canceled`,
#          `expired` and `status` on a received quote, taking it with `new` (an order naming it
#          in tag 117, any version), and `counter`
# Needs:   a session receiving quotes, FIX 4.4 for the counter: arm it on LOOP-CLI and run
#          quote-stream on LOOP-MKT
# Watch:   Received Quotes (Client menu): the Order column filling when the quote is taken;
#          Sent Orders for the order, PreviouslyQuoted
# Outcome: an IBM quote is countered ten cents under its offer; when a requote comes down to
#          150.05 or less it is taken for 100 with an order; a quote withdrawn or expired is
#          logged

on error continue

# The quote's row is `quote`; a stream of quotes on one symbol is one row,
# so a requote is an event of the same macro.
on quote where symbol == 'IBM'
    when requoted and quote.offer_px <= 150.05
        new symbol: quote.symbol, side: buy, qty: 100, type: previously_quoted, price: quote.offer_px
        stop
    when canceled or expired
        log '${quote.quote_id} gone: ${event.kind}'
        stop
    when status
        log 'status ${quote.quote_status}'
    counter offer: TICK(quote.offer_px - 0.10, 0.01)
